lease contact contact@cubic.dev.\u003c/sub\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\n\n\n\u003cfile name=\"botfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte\"\u003e\n\n\u003cviolation number=\"1\" location=\"botfn/docs/src/lib/components/DocsSiteSearch.svelte:2\"\u003e\nP3: `Search.svelte` is imported via a five-level relative path that ","state":"COMMENTED"},{"author":"pullfrog","body":"\u003e ✅ No new issues found in the new commit. The previous review thread remains open.\n\n**Reviewed changes** The follow-up commit moved the site runtime into shared code and replaced the search UI while narrowing the layout payload.\n\n- **Shared runtime:** Extracted the bundled provider and compiled-content cache into a per-site factory, with aliases for the site's DocsFn installation.\n- **Search and layout:** Replaced the published search dialog with a native modal, kept the search artifact on the server, and sent only site metadata to the layout.\n- **Responsive navigation:** Added a mobile sidebar display override and retained the existing docs route behavior.\n\n\u003c!--\nPullfrog review metadata. These findings were written against 18f71771;\nif commits have landed on codex/docs-botfn-20260926 since, treat every specific bug, file, or\nline callout as POTENTIALLY STALE and re-diff before acting o","state":"COMMENTED"},{"author":"cubic-dev-ai","body":"\u003c!-- cubic:review-summary:start --\u003e\n**1 existing issue remains and 2 new issues found across 30 files (changes from recent commits).**\n\u003c!-- cubic:review-summary:end --\u003e\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003ePrompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of ea